# Not needed at runtime — evaluation/, tests/, ui/, and datasets/ are
# development-only. Keeping them out of the build context also keeps
# `gcloud run deploy --source .` / Cloud Build upload fast.
#
# tools/ and training/ are NOT in this list, on purpose, even though most of
# each genuinely is dev-only:
#   - inference/squat_ai_mvp.py and inference/pushup_ai_mvp.py import
#     resample_sequence from tools/squat_ai/prepare_rehab24_squat.py.
#   - inference/squat_ai_mvp.py, pushup_ai_mvp.py, lunge_ai_mvp.py, and
#     application/squat_shadow.py import v2_segments from
#     training/squat_rep_boundary_v2.py; squat_ai_mvp.py also imports
#     load_checkpoint_strict from training/squat_correctness.py.
# Excluding either directory reproduced a real
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tools'` (or 'training') on every
# single container start, since application.workers unconditionally imports
# inference.squat_ai_mvp regardless of which exercise family is requested —
# confirmed by hiding each directory locally and importing api.main.
# .git/ intentionally NOT excluded: Dockerfile.runpod reads .git/HEAD at
# build time to bake a GIT_SHA deployment-integrity fingerprint into the
# image (see api/config.py's GIT_SHA / api/main.py's /health, /ping) —
# excluding it would silently defeat the one thing that proves what source
# actually built a given running image.
.github/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

evaluation/
tests/
ui/
datasets/
archive/
docs/
results/
splits/

# Desktop-only entry point (imports tkinter). ui/ above (which imports
# PIL.ImageTk) is the only other tkinter-coupled code, and it's already excluded.
run_application.py

# Local dev artifacts, never part of the image.
.env
*.log
prototype_store/
